 # rather than of what is on disk. The cost of that stronger property is that
 # the checkout has to be deterministic, and by default it is not. Git for
 # Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, so
-# the identical commit produced a different identity there. Measured:
+# the identical commit produced a different identity there. Measured on the
